    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "STOMP over WebSocket support is available in the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "spring-messaging"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "spring-websocket"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " modules. Once you have those dependencies, you can expose a STOMP endpoint over WebSocket, as the following example shows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "include-code::./WebSocketConfiguration[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "For the built-in simple broker, the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "/topic"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "/queue"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " prefixes do not have any special meaning. They are merely a convention to differentiate between pub-sub versus point-to-point messaging (that is, many subscribers versus one consumer). When you use an external broker, check the STOMP page of the broker to understand what kind of STOMP destinations and prefixes it supports."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "note"
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "To connect from a browser, for STOMP, you can use "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "stomp-js/stompjs"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              }
            ],
            "kind": "link",
            "target": "https://github.com/stomp-js/stompjs"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " which is the most actively maintained JavaScript library."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The following example code is based on it:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "const stompClient = new StompJs.Client({\n       brokerURL: 'ws://domain.com/portfolio',\n       onConnect: () => {\n           // ...\n       }\n   });"
          }
        ],
        "language": "javascript",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Alternatively, if you connect through SockJS, you can enable the "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "SockJS Fallback"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "web/websocket/fallback.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " on server-side with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "registry.addEndpoint(\"/portfolio\").withSockJS()"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and on JavaScript side, by following "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "those instructions"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "link",
            "target": "https://stomp-js.github.io/guide/stompjs/rx-stomp/using-stomp-with-sockjs.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Note that "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "stompClient"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " in the preceding example does not need to specify "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "login"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "passcode"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " headers. Even if it did, they would be ignored (or, rather, overridden) on the server side. See "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Connecting to a Broker"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "web/websocket/stomp/handle-broker-relay-configure.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Authentication"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "web/websocket/stomp/authentication.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " for more information on authentication."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
